## Domains and their boundaries

<% if layout == :domains -%>
_This app was generated with `--domains`. For each domain: what it owns, what it `exposes`, what it
`depends_on`, what it `publishes_events`, and — the part only prose can carry — **why the boundary
is where it is**._

The enforceable version of this section lives in `domains/<name>/domain.rb` and is printed by
`magik domains --json`. If the two disagree, the code is right and this file is stale.
<% else -%>
_This app is **flat**: everything in `app/<kind>/`, no `domains/` directory._

That is the right shape until more than one team owns parts of `app/`, or `app/models/` passes ~25
models, or two features have started reaching into each other's data. Record here which of those
signals you are watching for, so the move happens on evidence rather than on a feeling.

The move itself is mechanical — `git mv` into `domains/<name>/app/…` plus one `domain.rb` per
domain. Nothing inside a moved file changes.
<% end -%>

## Money

_Does money change hands? If so, whose?_

Two flows are easy to conflate and must never share a file:

| Flow | Lives in | Is |
|---|---|---|
| <%= app_title %> charging its own customers | `billing` in `config/app.rb` | subscriptions, plans, trials |
| <%= app_title %>'s customers charging theirs | `app/ledgers/` | double-entry, append-only, balanced at boot |

_If neither applies, write "no money" here and delete the table. An unused ledger is a liability._

